---
/* Home §01. The design system's photo-led hero: the declaration, the offer and the two actions
   all sit in one solid bone capsule laid over the photograph's left quiet field — the shape
   guidelines/photo-treatment.html specimens as CORRECT.

   The capsule carries the REAL hero copy rather than the specimen's "Somebody owns Monday
   morning.", so the band has one display voice instead of two. That is the whole reason this
   works: the previous arrangement kept the declaration above and put a second display line in the
   capsule, which stacked to a 1892px band and pushed the photograph below the fold on every
   desktop viewport.

   The declaration is set at clamp(38px,4.4vw,76px), down from clamp(52px,7.6vw,134px). It has to
   be: the capsule is 62% of the frame, and 134px type inside it wraps to four or five words a
   line. This is the real trade — the hero gains a photograph and loses roughly half its type
   scale. Judge the two against each other, not the type alone.

   No caption under this one, unlike every other photograph on the site. The sentence said the
   image is a generated illustration, which the ILLUSTRATIVE stamp beside it already says, and in
   the hero it was a line of mono under the fold-defining picture earning nothing. The stamp still
   renders and is still registered as home-photo-operations-leader in src/copy/claim-artefacts.ts,
   so the release gate still fails if the disclosure disappears — dropping the caption is a
   presentation choice, not a retreat from saying what the image is.

   On a phone the capsule leaves the image and goes ABOVE it (photo--capsule-first in
   EditorialPhoto), because a hero whose first screen is a photograph and whose headline is
   underneath has buried the thing the visitor came to read.

   The register's copy is still in src/copy/pages/home.ts (PORTFOLIO_ROWS and the HERO.register*
   keys), unused, in case it should reappear somewhere else rather than be deleted. */
import Folio from '../../ui/Folio.astro';
import Button from '../../ui/Button.astro';
import Declaration from '../../patterns/Declaration.astro';
import PhotoHero from '../../patterns/PhotoHero.astro';
import { HERO } from '../../../copy/pages/home';
import { OPERATIONS_LEADER, CAPSULES } from '../../../copy/photography';
import operationsLeader from '../../../assets/photography/hero-operations-leader-v1.png';
---

<PhotoHero
  image={operationsLeader}
  alt={OPERATIONS_LEADER.alt}
  focus={OPERATIONS_LEADER.focus}
  labelledBy="hero-heading"
>
  <div class="hero__lede">
    <Folio text={HERO.folio} />

    <Declaration
      as="h1"
      id="hero-heading"
      size="clamp(38px,4.4vw,76px)"
      leading="0.86"
      tracking="-0.035em"
      weight={900}
    >
      {HERO.headingLine1}<br />{HERO.headingLine2Before}<span class="hero__pull"
        >{HERO.headingPull}</span
      >{HERO.headingLine2After}
    </Declaration>

    <p class="hero__support">{HERO.support}</p>

    <div class="hero__actions">
      <Button href={HERO.primary.href} size="lg">{HERO.primary.label}</Button>
      <Button href={HERO.secondary.href} size="lg" variant="secondary">
        {HERO.secondary.label}
      </Button>
    </div>
  </div>
</PhotoHero>

<style>

  /* Violation 1 of 2: the display word breaks the left edge. */
  .hero__pull {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-left: -0.06em;
    color: var(--orange-press);
  }

  .hero__support {
    margin: clamp(18px, 2vw, 28px) 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(16px, 1.15vw, 21px);
    line-height: 1.4;
    max-width: 46ch;
  }

  .hero__actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: clamp(20px, 2.2vw, 32px);
  }
</style>
